10.	How can you use the tee command to append output to a file instead of overwriting it?
🔹 Command Syntax:
command | tee -a filename
•	command → any command whose output you want to capture.
•	| → pipe symbol, sends the output of the command to tee.
•	-a → append to the file instead of overwriting.
•	filename → the file where output is stored.
 
🔹 Example:
echo "New log entry" | tee -a output.log
•	This appends "New log entry" to output.log without deleting the existing content.
•	The output is also displayed on the terminal

